{
 "contexts": [
  {
   "slug": "deliberative-bodies",
   "title": "Deliberative bodies",
   "definition": "How any body that meets and decides together (a nonprofit board, a council or commission, an advisory group, an association's members, or a committee of any of these) is organized: its committees and who sits on them, the numbers its bylaws or charter set, what is asked for an agenda, what is minuted and the follow-ups a meeting assigns. Board-only matters stay in board-governance; government lawmaking stays in civic-legislation."
  }
 ],
